-- A section-level GIVEN (R4): a name declared once for a whole section,
-- instead of being repeated in every rule's own GIVEN.
--
-- The taught spelling is on the line after the heading, indented past the §.
-- A GIVEN at column 1 is still the next declaration's signature, as it always
-- was.
--
-- In this release a section binder evaluates as an assumed term, exactly like
-- ASSUME: a rule that reads one cannot be evaluated to a value until the binder
-- is supplied. It does appear in the export schema as a required request
-- parameter, which is what the .schema.golden beside this file shows.
--
-- Read that golden with one thing in mind: `surcharge` carries a TYPICALLY and
-- so has a JSON Schema `default`, yet is still listed in `required`. That is
-- today's ASSUME behaviour, inherited deliberately; making a TYPICALLY
-- parameter optional is separate, later work, so this is not a difference to
-- "fix".

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `applicable rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The rate that applies to this transaction
          surcharge IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

@export Tax on an amount
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER @desc The amount being taxed
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tax on` amount MEANS
    amount TIMES `applicable rate` PLUS surcharge

#CHECK `tax on`
